 endothermy, and dinosaur extinction: is there a connection?</article-title><source>Fungal Genet Biol</source><year>2005</year><volume>42</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>98</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.fgb.2004.11.008</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15670708</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Casadevall</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Steenbergen</surname><given-names>JN</given-names></name><name><surname>Nosanchuk</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><article-title>'Ready made' virulence and 'dual use' virulence factors in pathogenic environmental fungi &#x02013; the Cryptococcus neoformans paradigm</article-title><source>Curr Opin Microbiol</source><year>2003</year><volume>6</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>332</fpage><lpage>337</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1369-5274(03)00082-1</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12941400</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Luo</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Tucker</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Casadevall</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><article-title>Fc- and complement-receptor activation stimulates cell cycle progression of macrophage cells from G1 to S</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><year>2005</year><volume>174</volume><issue>11</issue><fpage>7226</fpage><lpage>7233</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15905568</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Retini</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kozel</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Pietrella</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Monari</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bistoni</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Vecchiarelli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><article-title>Interdependency of interleukin-10 and interleukin-12 in regulation of T-cell differentiation and effector function of monocytes in response to stimulation with Cryptococcus neoformans</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2001</year><volume>69</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>6064</fpage><lpage>6073</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11553544</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/IAI.69.10.6064-6073.2001</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Monari</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Baldelli</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Pietrella</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Retini</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tascini</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Francisci</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bistoni</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Vecchiarelli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><article-title>Monocyte dysfunction in patients with acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS) versus Cryptococcus neoformans</article-title><source>J Infect</source><year>1997</year><volume>35</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>257</fpage><lpage>263</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0163-4453(97)93042-5</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9459399</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Levitz</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Harrison</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Tabuni</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><article-title>Chloroquine induces human mononuclear phagocytes to inhibit and kill Cryptococcus neoformans by a mechanism independent of iron deprivation</article-title>